        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(store): order hydration observations durably",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- order canonical thread state, accepted evidence, child hydration, and workflow-run snapshots by GitHub source revision before local pre-fetch generation\n- allow a delayed newer source snapshot to replace an older snapshot even when it allocated a lower local generation\n- reject delayed stale hydration before it overwrites comments, PR details, documents, summaries, embeddings, or cluster inputs\n- converge supported schema-4/6/8/9/10 stores to one canonical schema with atomic rollback, exact stored-DDL checks, and a byte-stable healthy-v10 fast path\n- reject and repair the unrepresentable minimum-int64 observation sequence\n\n## Validation\n\nValidated at `1e3b0c0`:\n\n- `go test ./... -count=1`\n- `go test -race ./... -count=1`\n- `go vet ./...`\n- `go run golang.org/x/tools/cmd/deadcode@v0.45.0 -test ./...`\n- `make generate-sqlc` followed by a clean generated diff\n- `go mod tidy` followed by a clean module diff\n- delayed-newer parent/child interleaving repeated `200` times\n- evidence, reservation, migration, and overlapping-sync adversarial suites repeated `20-50` times\n- two-repository legacy-row regression proves summary tasks, summary-backed embeddings, and cluster summary lookup remain repository/thread scoped\n\n## Exact-head migration proof\n\n- used the real released `v0.7.1` schema-4 SQLite archive containing repository, PR, revision, file, and workflow-run rows\n- opened that archive through the exact `1e3b0c0` writable path: schema advanced from `4` to `10`, `pragma integrity_check` returned `ok`, foreign-key violations were `0`, and all seeded rows survived\n- compared complete ordered `sqlite_schema` output from the migrated archive with a fresh schema-10 archive; the diff was `0` bytes and both hashes were `9ad99a8aca9ba72ad582b9ffa6000f98edb549d093df8d92770f36c350ed397c`\n- verified the migrated schema carries source-revision ordering state for accepted evidence, every thread child family, and repository/head-SHA workflow reservations\n- prior exact-head proofs also cover healthy-v10 byte stability, allocator recovery, read-only diagnostics, and minimum-int64 repair\n\n## Review closeout\n\n- fixed the final concurrency finding where a delayed newer parent could be accepted while its complete evidence and children were rejected by a higher local sequence from an older source\n- the reproducer now blocks after parent fetch and sequence allocation, lets the older source commit first, then proves the newer source wins consistently across parent, evidence, all child families, and workflow runs\n- prior foreign-key rollback, malformed-schema, minimum-int64, and ungrouped freshness-disjunction findings remain regression-covered\n- final-head GitHub checks and two exact-range reviews are required before merge\n",
